course: dictionary
lesson: 7433
title: Pollination
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pollination is the moving of pollen from the male part of a flower, called the anther, to the female part, called the stigma. Once pollen lands on the stigma, seeds can begin to form.
explain: Read the words around it for clues. «Pollination happens when pollen gets carried from the stamens to the sticky top of a pistil.» The pollen moves from one part of a flower to another, and the sticky top is where it has to land. So pollination must mean that carrying of pollen.
explain: The sentence also tells you who does the carrying: «bees, butterflies, birds and the wind». Insects, birds and the wind all move pollen, so pollination is the job that helps flowers make seeds.
fact: Pollination means moving pollen from the anther to the stigma so that seeds can form.
fact: Insects such as bees, butterflies and hoverflies carry pollen from flower to flower while they drink nectar.
fact: Some plants, such as grasses and many trees, are pollinated by the wind.
fact: After pollination comes fertilisation, and then seeds and fruit.
fact: Without pollination many fruits and vegetables would not grow, which is why protecting bees matters.
exercise: What does pollination mean? | *Moving pollen from the anther to the stigma so that seeds can form | Opening a flower in the morning | Growing a new flower from a seed in the soil | Drinking nectar from a flower
exercise: Which of these carries pollen from flower to flower? | A pencil | A stone | *A bee | A puddle
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the male part of a flower. | nectar | *anther | seed | stigma
test: Which of these is NOT a way that pollen can be carried? | Birds | Butterflies | *A closed door | The wind
test: Some plants are pollinated by the wind. Which plant is most likely wind-pollinated? | A rose | A bluebell | *Grass | A poppy
exam: According to «Bats ... are very important for pollination and eating insects», why are bats valuable? | They grow the flowers themselves | They are a kind of fish | They make honey for bees | *They help with pollination and eat insects
